 "notes": "Parameter-sweep paper: one spine (processing -> internal porosity -> release) repeated over five variables; each variable's readouts are collapsed into p6/p10 with the variable in attrs. p6 (porosity) and p7 (BSA distribution) are read from the SAME CLSM contrast (bright = BSA, dark = void): in practice indistinguishable here, see merge comments. Figures opened: F2, F5, F9, F10. F2 caption (B = 0.1%) disagrees with text (0.5%). q7 is a text-silent audit: plateaus at ~50% and ~7% mean most protein is not released in 40 d, which qualifies the sustained-release performance claim. q3->p14 uses correlate_across_series (larger spheres co-vary with faster release across the external-PVA series), a correlational comparison with Roy et al."
}